---
title: Before you start
description: Who can set up workspaces and case templates, how to choose the interface language and how to create the department first.
sidebar:
  order: 1
---

A case template describes how one kind of case runs: its sections, the tasks in each section, who does each task and when each task is due. Cases are then started from the template on the workspace's **Cases** board.

**Who:** tenant admin. Only a tenant admin can create a department workspace. A manager can also select **Add new workspace**, but can create only a **Cross-department workspace**: the **Department workspace** option is unavailable, because choosing a department needs department management rights. Case templates are created by a tenant admin or a user who has been given **Template access**.

A department workspace needs its department first, and each department can have one workspace. This chapter uses the department `Sample After-sales` as the example; the steps are the same for any department.

## The chapters

1. Before you start (this page)
2. [Create a workspace](/en/case-templates/workspace/)
3. [Create a case template](/en/case-templates/create-template/)
4. [Set up sections and tasks](/en/case-templates/sections-tasks/)
5. [Template details and saving](/en/case-templates/details-save/)
6. [Start a case from the template](/en/case-templates/start-case/)

## Choose your interface language

Open **Settings** › **Language & region** and choose **English** or **中文** in the **Language** list. The choice is saved at once and the whole interface changes to that language; you do not need to sign in again. The language is your own setting: it does not change the language of other users.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/language-settings" caption="Choosing the interface language." /%}

## Open the department list

Go to **Admin** › **Departments**.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/departments-list" caption="The department list." /%}

## Create the department

{% steps %}

1. Select **+ New department**.
2. In **Name**, enter the department name, for example `Sample After-sales`. Leave **Parent** as **None (top level)**.
3. Select **Create**.

{% /steps %}

{% screenshot id="case-templates/department-new" caption="Creating a department." /%}

## The department is ready

The new department now appears in the list. You can create its workspace next.

{% screenshot id="case-templates/department-created" caption="The new department in the list." /%}

{% aside type="note" title="Examples in this chapter" %}
All firms, companies, people and templates in this chapter are fictional. The example firm is SAMPLE ACCOUNTING FIRM, the example users are Demo Accountant and Demo Manager, and the example client is ABC PTE. LTD.
{% /aside %}
